---
import SubPage from '../../layouts/SubPage.astro';
import { DOCS_SIDEBAR } from '../../lib/sidebar-data';

const currentPath = '/docs/install';
---

<SubPage
  title="Install · Pace"
  description="Install Pace plugins in Claude Code (terminal), the Cowork desktop app, or via the npx pace CLI. Step-by-step setup for engineers and non-technical users, plus connector authorization."
  activeNav="docs"
  canonicalPath={currentPath}
  sidebarLabel="Docs"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    {DOCS_SIDEBAR.map((group) => (
      <div class="subpage-sidebar-group">
        <span class="subpage-sidebar-group-title">{group.title}</span>
        <ul class="subpage-sidebar-list">
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={item.href}
                aria-current={item.href === currentPath ? 'page' : undefined}
              >{item.label}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </Fragment>

  <article class="installpage">
    <header class="installpage-header">
      <span class="installpage-eyebrow">Get started</span>
      <h1>Install Pace</h1>
      <p class="installpage-lede">
        Pace is a Claude Code plugin marketplace. Two install paths, both first-class: <strong>Cowork</strong> (the Claude desktop app) for click-to-install, and the <strong>Claude Code CLI</strong> for terminal-driven flows. Same plugins, same end state, different surface.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="installpage-paths">
      <a class="installpage-path installpage-path-cowork" href="#cowork">
        <span class="installpage-path-label">Click to install</span>
        <h3>Cowork (desktop)</h3>
        <p>One link per plugin. Cowork opens, asks you to confirm. No terminal, no commands. Right path if you don't write code for a living.</p>
        <span class="installpage-path-cta">Show me &darr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="installpage-path installpage-path-claude" href="#claude-code">
        <span class="installpage-path-label">Run in terminal</span>
        <h3>Claude Code (CLI)</h3>
        <p>Three commands: register the marketplace, install the plugins your team uses, connect tools on first run. Right path if you live in the terminal.</p>
        <span class="installpage-path-cta">Show me &darr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <nav class="installpage-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="installpage-toc-label">On this page</span>
      <ol class="installpage-toc-list">
        <li><a href="#cowork">Cowork (click-to-install)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#claude-code">Claude Code (terminal)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#picking">Picking plugins</a></li>
        <li><a href="#pace-cli">The <code>pace-tools</code> CLI</a></li>
        <li><a href="#updating">Updating</a></li>
        <li><a href="#verifying">Verifying it worked</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="cowork">
      <h2>Cowork (click-to-install)</h2>
      <p>
        Cowork is the Claude desktop app: a graphical interface to the same plugin ecosystem Claude Code uses in the terminal. Same plugins, same end state, different surface. In Cowork you click a link instead of typing a command.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Install Cowork</h3>
      <p>Download from <a href="https://claude.com/product/cowork" target="_blank" rel="noopener">claude.com/product/cowork</a> and sign in with your Anthropic account.</p>

      <h3>2. Click an install link per plugin</h3>
      <p>
        Each plugin has a deep link that opens Cowork and adds the Pace marketplace plus the plugin in a single step.
      </p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code><span class="installpage-comment"># Pattern</span>
https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&amp;plugin=&lt;name&gt;

<span class="installpage-comment"># Examples</span>
https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&amp;plugin=sales
https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&amp;plugin=marketing
https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&amp;plugin=engineering</code></pre>
      <p>
        Cowork prompts you to confirm the install. Want a curated set per role? The <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> have one-click install buttons for sales, marketing, engineering, finance, and the rest.
      </p>

      <div class="installpage-callout installpage-callout-warning">
        <strong>Restart Cowork after the last install.</strong> The MCP servers (Slack, HubSpot, Notion, etc.) only register cleanly on a fresh app start. Quit the app completely (Cmd+Q on macOS), then reopen it. If your <code>/</code> menu doesn't show the new commands, this is almost always the fix.
      </div>

      <h3>3. Authorize connectors when prompted</h3>
      <p>
        The first time a skill needs an external tool (Slack, HubSpot, Notion, etc.), Cowork opens an OAuth window. Sign in once per service, approve the scope, and the connector stays authorized for every plugin that uses it.
      </p>

      <div class="installpage-callout">
        <strong>Rolling Pace out to a non-technical team.</strong> Install Cowork on each user's machine and send them a shortlist of deep links for the plugins they need. Each person authorizes connectors against their own accounts, so HR sees only HR's HubSpot, sales sees only sales's HubSpot, and so on.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="claude-code">
      <h2>Claude Code (terminal)</h2>
      <p>
        If you live in the terminal, three commands get you the same end state Cowork does. No config files to edit, no API keys to manage.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Register the marketplace</h3>
      <p>One-time per machine. Tells Claude Code where to find Pace's catalog.</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>claude plugin marketplace add GoldenBerry-SO/Pace</code></pre>
      <p class="installpage-aside">
        Claude Code clones the GitHub repo and reads its <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/blob/main/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json">marketplace.json</a>. The marketplace registers as <code>pace</code>; you install plugins with the <code>@pace</code> suffix.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Install the plugins your team uses</h3>
      <p>Install one plugin per team or function. The router (<code>pace</code>) is optional but recommended; it's where your company-specific commands go.</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code><span class="installpage-comment"># The router (company commands like /pace teach)</span>
claude plugin install pace@pace

<span class="installpage-comment"># Department plugins (install only what you use)</span>
claude plugin install sales@pace
claude plugin install engineering@pace
claude plugin install data@pace
claude plugin install marketing@pace</code></pre>
      <p>
        Not sure which to install? See <a href="#picking">Picking plugins</a> below, or jump to the <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> for role-based recommendations.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Connect your tools (on first use)</h3>
      <p>
        Plugins ship with connectors but they're not authorized yet. The first time you run a skill that needs Slack, HubSpot, Notion, or any other MCP server, Claude opens an OAuth flow in your browser. Sign in, approve, and the token is saved for next time.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the full connector model (OAuth, self-hosted URLs, local stdio servers), see <a href="/docs/connectors">Connectors &amp; MCP</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="picking">
      <h2>Picking plugins</h2>
      <p>
        Pace ships 50 plugins. Most teams install three to six. Two ways to pick:
      </p>

      <h3>By role</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> have starter sets for sales, marketing, engineering, data, product, design, finance, legal, operations, people, customer support, and productivity. Each guide lists the plugins to install and a sample week of commands.
      </p>

      <h3>By plugin</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/plugins">plugin catalog</a> shows every plugin with its skills, connectors, and intended audience. Browse it like an app store.
      </p>

      <p class="installpage-aside">
        Installing more plugins isn't free: each one adds skills to your <code>/</code> menu and bytes to the agent's context. Start with the few that map to your weekly work and add more as you find gaps.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="pace-cli">
      <h2>The <code>pace-tools</code> CLI</h2>
      <p>
        Pace ships a small Node CLI you can run with <code>npx</code>. It's a thin wrapper around <code>claude plugin</code>, useful when you want to install many plugins at once or script the setup for an onboarding flow.
      </p>

      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code><span class="installpage-comment"># One-time: register the Pace marketplace with Claude Code</span>
npx pace-tools marketplace add

<span class="installpage-comment"># Install one or more plugins</span>
npx pace-tools install sales
npx pace-tools install engineering data

<span class="installpage-comment"># Browse the full catalog</span>
npx pace-tools list

<span class="installpage-comment"># See per-role starter sets</span>
npx pace-tools teams
npx pace-tools teams sales

<span class="installpage-comment"># What's installed?</span>
npx pace-tools status

<span class="installpage-comment"># Remove a plugin</span>
npx pace-tools uninstall sales</code></pre>

      <div class="installpage-callout">
        <strong>Requires Claude Code.</strong> The CLI wraps <code>claude plugin install</code>, so the <code>claude</code> binary must be on PATH. If you only use Cowork, install through the deep links above instead.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="updating">
      <h2>Updating</h2>

      <h3>Claude Code</h3>
      <p>Refresh the marketplace; reinstall plugins to pick up the new versions:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>claude plugin marketplace update pace
claude plugin install &lt;name&gt;@pace      <span class="installpage-comment"># reinstalls; picks up new version</span></code></pre>

      <h3>Cowork</h3>
      <p>Cowork pulls plugin updates from the marketplace whenever you reopen the app or re-run a plugin install link. The exact in-app update UI is app-version dependent; see Cowork's docs for the current flow.</p>

      <h3>Pace CLI</h3>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>npx pace-tools status     <span class="installpage-comment"># what's installed + which marketplaces are registered</span></code></pre>
      <p>Re-run <code>npx pace-tools install &lt;name&gt;</code> after a marketplace refresh to upgrade a plugin.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="verifying">
      <h2>Verifying it worked</h2>
      <p>
        Open a chat in Claude Code or Cowork and type <code>/</code>. You should see commands prefixed by the plugins you installed: <code>/sales:call-prep</code>, <code>/engineering:standup</code>, <code>/pace:teach</code>, etc. Type one and the corresponding skill takes over.
      </p>
      <p>
        Connectors stay <em>declared but not authorized</em> until the first skill that needs them runs. That's by design: authorization is just-in-time, so a fresh install doesn't barrage you with OAuth windows you don't need yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stuck? Open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues">github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SubPage>

<style>
  .installpage {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .installpage-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .installpage-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .installpage-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .installpage-lede a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-paths {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .installpage-paths {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .installpage-path {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-path:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 88%, var(--color-forest-dim));
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .installpage-path-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-path h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .installpage-path p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-path-cta {
    margin-top: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .installpage-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .installpage-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px var(--spacing-md);
    counter-reset: toc;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li {
    counter-increment: toc;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li::before {
    content: counter(toc, decimal-leading-zero) ' ';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a:hover {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-color: var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .installpage-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .installpage-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section ol,
  .installpage-section ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .installpage-section a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-section a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-section strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .installpage-pre {
    background: oklch(18% 0.015 150);
    color: oklch(92% 0.005 150);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-pre code {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-comment {
    color: oklch(62% 0.04 150);
  }
  .installpage-aside {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-style: italic;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-left: 2px;
  }
  .installpage-aside a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-callout {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-forest);
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-callout strong {
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning {
    background: var(--color-clay-dim);
    border-left-color: var(--color-clay);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning strong {
    color: var(--color-clay-hover);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .installpage-toc-list {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
